import JinWishartFormalization.TwoRowGramSupport

open JinWishart

/- Auxiliary lemmas supplied by Codex (not generated by the local model):
twoRowGramChart_determinant (p) (hp : 0 < p 0) :
  chart p 0 * chart p 3 - (chart p 1)^2 - (chart p 2)^2 = p 0 * p 3
  where chart = twoRowGramChart.
twoRowGramChart_right_inverse (q) (hq : 0 < q 0) :
  twoRowGramChart (twoRowGramChartInverse q) = q
twoRowGramChart_inverse_residual_pos (q) (hq : 0 < q 0)
  (hd : q 1^2 + q 2^2 < q 0*q 3) : 0 < twoRowGramChartInverse q 3

Use these exact lemmas; no square-root algebra remains.
Forward: unpack the image witness p, substitute q=chart p, use mul_pos on
the two positive energies, then nlinarith with the determinant identity.
Reverse: witness twoRowGramChartInverse q, whose coordinate 0 is q 0 by
simp [twoRowGramChartInverse]; residual positivity and chart equality follow
from the supplied lemmas. Use Set.ext or Set.Subset.antisymm. -/
theorem twoRowGramChart_positive_image :
    twoRowGramChart '' {p : GramChartSpace | 0 < p 0 ∧ 0 < p 3} =
      {q : GramChartSpace | 0 < q 0 ∧ q 1 ^ 2 + q 2 ^ 2 < q 0 * q 3} := by
  sorry
